1
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:09,504
Marilyn, you want coffee or tea?

2
00:00:09,504 --> 00:00:24,763
Coffee, please.

3
00:00:24,763 --> 00:00:27,200
I am so excited!

4
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,736
At this time tomorrow morning,

5
00:00:28,736 --> 00:00:37,366
Grandpa will be sitting in the kitchen with us.

6
00:00:37,366 --> 00:00:39,067
When does he arrive?

7
00:00:39,067 --> 00:00:42,044
At six o'clock this evening.

8
00:00:42,044 --> 00:00:43,351
By plane?

9
00:00:43,351 --> 00:00:47,356
No, by train.

10
00:00:47,356 --> 00:00:49,897
Are we picking him up at the station?

11
00:00:49,897 --> 00:00:51,297
Not Grandpa.

12
00:00:51,297 --> 00:00:54,638
He doesn't want anybody picking him up.

13
00:00:54,638 --> 00:00:57,137
He likes to be independent.

14
00:00:57,137 --> 00:00:58,102
Huh.

15
00:00:58,102 --> 00:01:01,121
Oh, let's go upstairs and prepare Grandpa's room.

16
00:01:01,121 --> 00:01:04,741
Great! Let's do it!

17
00:01:04,741 --> 00:01:05,872
Good morning, Mom.

18
00:01:05,872 --> 00:01:06,691
Morning.

19
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:07,210
Well, hi, fellas.

20
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:07,843
Hello.

21
00:01:07,843 --> 00:01:08,195
Hi, honey.

22
00:01:08,195 --> 00:01:08,973
Morning, Marilyn.

23
00:01:08,973 --> 00:01:10,571
We are going upstairs to set up Grandpa's room.

24
00:01:10,571 --> 00:01:15,477
There's coffee ready.

25
00:01:15,477 --> 00:01:17,791
I'm really excited about seeing Grandpa.

26
00:01:17,791 --> 00:01:21,483
Me, too. Milk, please.

27
00:01:21,483 --> 00:01:22,687
He's so funny.

28
00:01:22,687 --> 00:01:26,846
He always makes me laugh.

29
00:01:26,846 --> 00:01:29,066
I hope Grandpa's going to like living with us.

30
00:01:29,066 --> 00:01:30,633
I think he will.

31
00:01:30,633 --> 00:01:33,153
It just takes time to feel comfortable in a new place.

32
00:01:33,153 --> 00:01:34,854
Won't he miss being in Florida?

33
00:01:34,854 --> 00:01:35,819
Well, he will.

34
00:01:35,819 --> 00:01:38,091
But I think he'll like being here with the family.

35
00:01:38,091 --> 00:01:39,429
Are you sure about that?

36
00:01:39,429 --> 00:01:41,151
It's crazy here most of the time.

37
00:01:41,151 --> 00:01:42,458
But it's fun.

38
00:01:42,458 --> 00:01:44,699
That's for sure.

39
00:01:44,699 --> 00:01:45,352
You know,

40
00:01:45,352 --> 00:01:47,800
maybe I'll put together some photos of Grandpa

41
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:49,221
as a "welcome" present.

42
00:01:49,221 --> 00:01:51,358
That's a neat idea.

43
00:01:51,358 --> 00:01:53,132
What can I do?

44
00:01:53,132 --> 00:01:54,190
I've got it!

45
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:58,993
I have a picture of Grandpa and Dad and me in my wallet.

46
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:00,891
It's from the Fathers and Sons' Breakfast

47
00:02:00,891 --> 00:02:03,578
at my junior high school graduation.

48
00:02:03,578 --> 00:02:07,841
Oh, I remember this picture.

49
00:02:07,841 --> 00:02:11,399
I'd really like to pick up Grandpa at the railroad station.

50
00:02:11,399 --> 00:02:13,702
Railroad stations or airports.

51
00:02:13,702 --> 00:02:16,472
Grandpa always tells us he'll get here by himself.

52
00:02:16,472 --> 00:02:23,277
He's something!

53
00:02:23,277 --> 00:02:25,922
Is this all Grandpa's stuff?

54
00:02:25,922 --> 00:02:27,291
That's it.

55
00:02:27,291 --> 00:02:32,032
But I'm sure he has a few bags with him on the train.

56
00:02:32,032 --> 00:02:35,559
What's inside?

57
00:02:35,559 --> 00:02:42,716
I don't know. It's locked.

58
00:02:42,716 --> 00:02:43,961
Hi.

59
00:02:43,961 --> 00:02:44,843
Oh, hi, darling.

60
00:02:44,843 --> 00:02:45,735
Morning, Philip.

61
00:02:45,735 --> 00:02:49,013
I want to put some of my good hangers in Grandpa's closet.

62
00:02:49,013 --> 00:02:52,467
You know I'm very excited about his arrival.

63
00:02:52,467 --> 00:02:54,459
We are, too.

64
00:02:54,459 --> 00:02:56,741
Susan called early this morning.

65
00:02:56,741 --> 00:02:57,653
She's unhappy

66
00:02:57,653 --> 00:03:00,994
because she's had to go to Chicago on a business trip

67
00:03:00,994 --> 00:03:02,664
and can't leave till tonight.

68
00:03:02,664 --> 00:03:04,593
She wants to be here for Grandpa.

69
00:03:04,593 --> 00:03:08,089
Well, Grandpa will be disappointed, too.

70
00:03:08,089 --> 00:03:09,883
He loves Susan.

71
00:03:09,883 --> 00:03:13,327
She always reminds him of Grandma.

72
00:03:13,327 --> 00:03:15,973
Well, how's everything here?

73
00:03:15,973 --> 00:03:23,026
Fine. We were just wondering about this trunk.

74
00:03:23,026 --> 00:03:24,323
It's locked.

75
00:03:24,323 --> 00:03:24,323
Oh. I have the key. Grandpa sent it to me.
